<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lausanne Disputation</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1536">1536</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lausanne">Lausanne</a> Disputation was a public religious debate held in Lausanne in October 1536, after Bern conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaud">Vaud</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guillaume-farel">Guillaume Farel</a>, Pierre Viret and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-calvin">John Calvin</a> defended the Reformed theses against Catholic speakers, and Bern used the outcome to impose the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> throughout Vaud and abolish the Mass.</p></div>
